From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] jails/instances/lab-mail: Carry the list instead of
 relaying it
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: vluqmqqoqzzvlrlyxmuloovpyvxmomqp
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:39:13 +0000

The list travels as a maildir in jj, so two sides that add mail
conflict, and agents reach new mail only through Pat's merge. This
turns lab-mail into the hub the spec describes, so every host can sync
the list over IMAP and post to it over SMTP, and Fastmail keeps a copy
of everything.

Dovecot becomes the only writer of the list. OpenSMTPD takes posts on
loopback, refuses a recipient it does not know and a message that is
not well formed while the client is still connected, and hands the
rest to Dovecot over LMTP. mbsync syncs lists and Archive both ways as
an IMAP client of Fastmail and of Dovecot, so neither it nor OpenSMTPD
touches the maildir. Readers can only read. Dovecot's ACL lets only
the two logins in imap-users, Pat and mbsync, change the list.

smtprelay, the fetch job, and the mailcred group go away with the
relay. A maildir the relay fetched must be emptied before the first
sync, since mbsync with no sync state would copy every message to the
other side again. README.org gives the setup, and the one-time import
of the jj maildir.
