+** import the jj maildir
+The list before lab-mail lived in the jj maildir on the =mail=
+bookmark. Once lab-mail's first sync has pulled =lists= and =Archive=
+from Fastmail, the operator imports that maildir into =lists= once,
+from beastie, as =pat@p7x.dev=. The next sync carries it to Fastmail.
+mbsync renames each file it syncs, so it reads a copy, never the jj
+working copy:
+#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
+cp -R ~/lab/mail.jj/maildir /tmp/list-import
+mkdir /tmp/list-import-state
+cat > /tmp/list-import.rc <<'EOF'
+IMAPAccount lab-mail
+Host 127.0.0.1
+Port 2143
+TLSType None
+AuthMechs LOGIN
+User pat@p7x.dev
+PassCmd "pass show lab-mail/pat@p7x.dev"
+
+IMAPStore lab-mail
+Account lab-mail
+
+MaildirStore import
+Path /tmp/
+Inbox /tmp/list-import
+
+Channel import
+Far :lab-mail:lists
+Near :import:
+Sync Push New
+Create None
+Expunge None
+Remove None
+CopyArrivalDate yes
+SyncState /tmp/list-import-state/
+EOF
+mbsync -c /tmp/list-import.rc import
+#+END_EXAMPLE
+
+A message that is already on Fastmail and in the jj maildir lands
+twice. notmuch indexes both files under the one Message-ID, so a
+thread shows it once.
